cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite the preprint below."
title: "Subsurface SAR Doppler Tomography: a controlled reproduction and refutation"
abstract: >-
  An independent, controls-first reproduction and refutation of the single-pass
  SAR Doppler micro-motion tomography method (Biondi & Malanga) used to claim
  deep subsurface structures beneath the Giza plateau. Open pipeline, controls,
  stress tests, and figure-generation scripts.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Foreman
    given-names: Hassan
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hassanforeman/subsurface-sar-tomo"
keywords:
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - SAR Doppler tomography
  - micro-motion
  - reproducibility
  - null result
  - remote sensing
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    No Reproducible Evidence for Deep Subsurface Structures Beneath the Giza
    Plateau: A Controlled Reproduction of Single-Source SAR Doppler Micro-Motion
    Tomography
  authors:
